{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3283","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3283","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3283\",\"parent_revision\":\"1d5be9359f7e1e80ad65c04749781dc6f3d51631ed0224dd07d1e74a317ece47\",\"root_revision\":\"1d5be9359f7e1e80ad65c04749781dc6f3d51631ed0224dd07d1e74a317ece47\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSurfaced by task T4 (plan Pb31107bf, dispatched for #3268) and independently verified during /dh:complete-implementation's Pre-Phase 1b concerns processing.\\n\\nT4 added a `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` section to `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` forbidding speculative conclusions and hedged language (naming \\\"likely\\\", \\\"probably\\\", \\\"seems\\\") in dispatch prompts, per architect spec \u00a74's verbatim text. T4's own CoVe check (spec \u00a74 note) found that `plugins/agent-orchestration/skills/agent-orchestration/SKILL.md` (around lines 73, 75-80) and `plugins/agent-orchestration/skills/delegate/SKILL.md:134` already state closely related guidance \u2014 agent-orchestration's SKILL.md instructs observation-only language and explicitly prohibits hedging words (\\\"I think\\\", \\\"probably\\\", \\\"likely\\\", \\\"seems\\\") in dispatch content, and delegate/SKILL.md's `review` phase table row establishes the same \\\"independent critique, do not pre-bias\\\" principle the new dispatch-contract rule protects.\\n\\nVerified directly: `plugins/agent-orchestration/skills/agent-orchestration/SKILL.md` around line 73 does contain observation-language guidance prohibiting \\\"hedging language or speculation such as \u2014 'I think', 'probably', 'likely', 'seems'\\\" \u2014 confirming T4's citation.\\n\\nThe new dispatch-contract text was written per the architect spec verbatim, referencing only its own agent-facing counterpart (subagent-contract's dispatch_input rule, from T3), without citing or deferring to the existing agent-orchestration/delegate prior art. Two independently-maintained texts across two plugins now assert overlapping dispatch-prompt-scope guidance with no cross-reference between them, which can drift out of sync over time (one gets updated, the other doesn't, and a reader following only one plugin's docs never learns the other exists).\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 whether the fix is a cross-reference from dispatch-contract to the agent-orchestration prior art, a merge into one canonical location, or something else is a design question for grooming, not decided here.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3268\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1b37ae33c068fa687daaf7823c35ad2031680009c11e0948340a292266274354\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSB8_w\"}"}